      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Admissions Officer Department/Faculty Student Services - Registrar's Office Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 year Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4712 Internal Closing Date: July 23, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 9 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $30.34 to $33.88 per hour Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 8:30am - 4:30pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking an Admissions Officer to join our Admissions and Transfer Credit team (Office of the Registrar). Job Overview The Admissions Officer (AO) is responsible for receiving, verifying and evaluating applications, transcripts and supporting documentation for admission and transfer credit in accordance with established policy and articulation agreements. The Admissions Officer advises applicants, students, faculty, and staff regarding resources and provide information regarding KPU admissions and transfer policies and procedures. The AO sends timely and accurate offers of admission, liaising with key parties across the institution, and verifying the completion of any conditions of admission. Education and Experience Successful completion of an undergraduate bachelor’s degree. Minimum 2 years of recent experience working in an admissions, transfer credit and/or enrolment service position within a Registrar’s Office. Minimum 2 years recent experience assessing secondary and post-secondary transcripts for admission and transfer credit, including applying approved articulations to student records. An applicable combination of education and experience may be considered. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated detailed knowledge of KPU programs as well as policies, procedures and processes relating to current application, admission and transfer credit. Demonstrated knowledge of BC and Canadian secondary and post-secondary education systems. Knowledge of international educational systems and credentials (secondary/post-secondary) considered an asset. Demonstrated experience and working knowledge of BC transfer system and transfer credit articulation processes for domestic and international credentials. Experience applying policies and procedures for determination of admission decisions, transfer credit articulation, and application of prior learning assessments. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing, with prospective and current students, faculty and staff across KPU. Formal training and/or extensive acquired knowledge of student information system database at an intermediate/advanced level. Ex: Banner Student. Ability to deal patiently and effectively with a diverse range of people and situations. Experience in dealing with sensitive situations that call for the use of diplomacy and tact in the delivery of information and explanations. Demonstrated proficiency at an intermediate level with Microsoft Office, including Excel, Word and Outlook. Customer service experience in a fast-paced work environment involving multiple demands and a diverse clientele. Demonstrated ability to handle confidential information appropriately. Demonstrated experience in planning and presenting training activities. Demonstrated ability to work independently, exercise good judgment and demonstrate initiative. Excellent organizational skills, including the ability to set priorities and meet deadlines. Demonstrated aptitude for exacting and precise work. Minimum of 40 WPM keyboarding skills with a high degree of accuracy. Demonstrated knowledge of basic math. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4724": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description AGC Research Technician Department/Faculty Applied Genomics Centre Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration Until March 31, 2027 Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4724 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Director, Applied Genomics Centre. SUMMARY The Research Technician has a supportive role for research goals of the Applied Genomics Centre (AGC). This individual will support applied research projects under the supervision and direction of the AGC Director, Laboratory and Research Coordinator, and senior research staff. Where appropriate, they may also help supervise and train student researchers working in the AGC laboratories, or in the field as applicable. They will contribute to experimental design, perform laboratory tasks, and communicate results to the Director, Associates, and industry partners. There are currently 2 openings for this position. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Provide research support for the AGC’s Director, Faculty project leads, Laboratory and Research Coordinator, and senior research staff Gather, organize and maintain experimental data and records in the AGC lab, and in the field when required Execute experiments required for research projects, including quality control, and troubleshooting when necessary Assist in preparing reports and presentations, collaboratively and under the direction of the AGC’s senior leadership Provide on-site supervision and training to undergraduate student researchers, when required Generate and update standard operating procedures for routine and new developments, in collaboration with the Laboratory and Research Coordinator and/or senior research staff Other duties as assigned QUALIFICATIONS BSc in Biology or related discipline Relevant experience with a focus on genomics and/or metabolomics Research experience is an asset *SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $24.00 - $28.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4791": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Appliance Servicing Instructor Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 (one) year on call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4791 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 3 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Qualified Faculty List Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): APPLIANCE SERVICE TECHNICIAN INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: QUALIFIED FACULTY LIST POSITION START: As soon as possible FACULTY OVERVIEW: The Appliance Service Technician program prepares students for entry into the appliance service and repair industry. Students complete all of the in-school training required for Red Seal qualifications and develop their skills through hands-on opportunities. Students also acquire a sound knowledge of common appliance systems and essential skills necessary to succeed in the industry. POSITION OVERVIEW: The Faculty of Trades and Technology is currently seeking a Non-regular Type 1 Appliance Service Technician Instructor to provide short-term coverage in the Appliance Service Technician program which may extend from a single day to several weeks, possibly leading to a regularized contract. Part of this contract may require the delivery of the BC Provincial Appliance Service Technician Gas Certificate. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: A BC Certificate of Qualification (BC TQ), or a Certificate of Qualification with Interprovincial Red Seal (IP RSE) from another jurisdiction. A BC Gas Certificate, or equivalent. A minimum of five years relevant, related, industry experience as an Appliance Service Journeyperson. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates will be required to undergo a Criminal Record Check. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, the Qualified Faculty List will be drawn upon to assign work. As such, please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4744": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Artist in Residence Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 3-6 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4744 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 4 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Associate Dean or designate. SUMMARY The Faculty of Arts invites applications from the KPU Entertainment Arts Alumni or current Entertainment Arts students for 1-4 positions as Artist in Residence. These residencies will work on projects initiated by KPU groups the KPU Creative Lab and collaborate with current Entertainment Arts students in creating content to develop, promote, and communicate the identified projects led by faculty. They will help contribute materials and assets to projects, attend meetings, and complete work as assigned related to the KPU Creative Lab. Working schedules for the Artist(s) in Residence may be flexible over the course of the project durations. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Attend weekly planning sessions with the faculty project lead as required Assist and elicit support from members to scope, plan, and execute their projects Work on assigned topics and tasks within the scope of the projects Provide/receive feedback to and from their project members Adhere to the Policies and Procedures of the university Establish and maintain effective relationships with administrators, peers, support staff, students and the community at large Participate in scheduled meetings and appropriate university-related activities as requested by the Dean or designate. QUALIFICATIONS Education and Experience Demonstrable familiarity and experience in one or more of the following disciplines: 3D Animation/3D Modelling VFX Game Development Graduated or current student from KPU Entertainment Arts Advanced VFX Program, Advanced 3D Animation and 3D Modelling Program, or Game Development Program Experience working in the industry and with students is advantageous Skills and Abilities Excellent communication, organizational, time management and interpersonal skills Critical thinking and problem-solving skills Ability to interpret and apply university, government, agency and departmental policies, procedures, and guidelines Ability to exercise a high level of initiative and responsibility Ability to use tact and discretion to deal with or settle complex requests Ability to communicate effectively and efficiently SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $45.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
