    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4717": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Faculty of Arts, Journalism and Communications Department/Faculty Office of the President Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 12 MONTHS Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4717 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 3 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): We are seeking a Student Assistant to support the Faculty of Arts, Journalism and Communications . The student will provide assistance in researching, interviewing, writing, and editing for the KPU 50th anniversary book project. PRINCIPAL DUTIES Fact-finding about KPU’s history and various individuals involved in KPU Interviewing people involved in KPU Transcribing interviews and writing profiles of people involved in KPU Editing other students’ written work Reviewing profiles with interviewees Creating and maintaining the project website and social media accounts REQUIREMENTS Strong written and verbal communication skills Must be a journalism or creative writing student Reliable and hardworking Familiarity with basic principles of web design and social media Interested in history and post-secondary education This position is reserved for KPU Students only. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4710": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Faculty of Arts - Indigenous Artist, Writer, Journalist, or Knowledge-Keeper in Residence Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 3-6 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4710 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): We are currently seeking an Indigenous Artist, Writer, Journalist, or Knowledge-Keeper in Residence to join our Faculty of Arts . ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Dean and Associate Dean, Faculty of Arts. SUMMARY The Faculty of Arts invites applications from established or emerging Indigenous artists, writers, musicians, and knowledge-keepers, including First Nations, Métis, and Inuit, for one position as Indigenous Artist, Writer, Musician, or Knowledge-Keeper in Residence. Please note other areas of focus not listed may also be considered. These residencies will support Indigenous knowledge in research and in the creation of new works in variety of fields, including but not restricted to Indigenous governance, health, pedagogy, sustainability, literary composition and spoken word, filmmaking, music, the visual arts (carving, weaving, painting, drawing, photography, digital media, sculpture, printmaking, etc.), performance and interdisciplinary creative practices. All residents will be able to divide their time between their own projects and contributing to the Faculty of Arts. In their application, candidates are encouraged to detail how they envision engaging with the Faculty of Arts (faculty, students, and staff) and the broader KPU community. For more information about the Faculty of Arts, please visit our website at: https://www.kpu.ca/arts . Residents will be paid $7,000 per month for the duration of their residency. There will also be some funding available for KPU-specific events and general support. We encourage applicants with a specialization in healing through culture or a wellness-related area. KPU is committed to the Truth and Reconciliation Commission (TRC) of Canada Calls to Actions and to supporting Indigenous writers and their representation and visibility within KPU and its broader communities. This program will foster community engagement and will have a positive impact on both the writers and the KPU community through sharing, dialogue, creativity, and intercultural communication. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The organization and hosting of a series of events for the Faculty of Arts and KPU that may include the following: a one-day symposium; craft talk; public readings; curated reading. Giving guest lectures and/or readings within the Faculty of Arts. Consulting with writers or artists of various abilities 2 days a week Meeting regularly with the Associate Dean and/or Dean, Faculty of Arts. Engaging with departments, and/or faculty, staff, and student groups in the Faculty of Arts and the broader KPU community. QUALIFICATIONS Relevant community-based and/or professional experience rooted in Indigenous communities, knowledge, and traditions. Writers should have at least one book published, or a book contract with a professional publishing house, or an equivalent major project in spoken or written text and have been active in their creative discipline(s). Artists/musician should be active in their creative discipline(s) with an established or emerging record of work as made evident through exhibitions, recordings, reviews, articles public performances, etc. Knowledge-keepers should have an active practice made evident through exhibitions and/or publication, community engagement, and written and/or oral research. Similar evidence of achievement in area of specialization. Enthusiasm for engaging with writers of various abilities. Willingness to organize and plan events. Enthusiasm for consulting with artists of various abilities. Ability to travel between campuses is required. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS Candidates are asked to submit: A curriculum vitae. A cover letter or video that includes your statement of interest; a proposal of the project; and a description of the kind of events you would like to plan and how you see these contributing to the KPU community. (For video submissions, please provide a link to a website or Google doc). A statement clearly indicating your availability to be present on KPU campuses (primarily the Surrey, Richmond, and/or Langley campuses) in the Spring 2026 or Summer 2026 semester. A letter of support or documentation regarding your connections to Indigenous community and/or an Indigenous organization, as well as lived experience. A writing sample of no more than 5 pages (if applicable). The names of two references. Please submit the application requirements listed above as one document via KPU's Career Centre . Click \"Career Opportunities\", search for this posting, and click \"Apply Now\". *SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $45.00 Does this role sound like it was made for you, yet you don’t check every box? We at KPU understand that experiences and qualifications may look differently for everyone and, if this job description is of interest to you, we encourage you to apply. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4765": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Human Resources Associate Department/Faculty Human Resources Home Campus (Location) Langley, BC Employment Duration 8 Months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4765 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 5 – Administrative Salary Grid - $63,156 to $88,418 Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Administration/Management Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): We are currently seeking a Human Resources Associate to join our Human Resources team. Job Overview Reporting to the Director, Workforce Advisory and Compensation, the Human Resources Associate is responsible for providing prompt, accurate and confidential service and support to employees of the University regarding Human Resources issues. The role is responsible for compiling, documenting, entering and updating employee and job information in the HRIS.  The role provides information, advice and guidance to employees regarding relevant collective agreements, policies, and benefits and supports Business Leaders with contract questions. Education and Experience Diploma in Business Administration or related field of study. A minimum of two years’ related experience, preferably within a unionized environment. Or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Demonstrated working knowledge of complex Human Resources/Payroll systems such as Banner, PeopleSoft and SAP. Demonstrated working knowledge Microsoft Office. Experience handling HR processes and issues related to benefits, recruiting and employee relations. Proven ability to adapt to changes in the work environment, manage competing demands and to deal with change, delays or unexpected events, keeping constant sight of the overall objectives couple with strong organizational skills. Demonstrated aptitude for exacting and precise work, including ability to perform arithmetic calculations accurately. Experience identifying and resolving problems in a timely manner and gathering and analyzing information skillfully. Experience presenting data and information in a concise, clear and meaningful manner to individuals and small groups. Demonstrated ability to work independently, take initiative and overcome obstacles. Proven ability to recognize and maintain highest levels of confidentiality. Ability to maintain poise and professionalism in all types of situations. Ability to travel between campuses is required. Competencies Leadership : KPU employees inspire, coach, mentor, and support students, employees and KPU as a whole in achieving objectives. Accountability : KPU employees demonstrate fiscal accountability and take ownership for their actions, decisions and results. Continuous Improvement : KPU employees take a creative approach to opportunities, exploring unique ways to create optimal value for the KPU community. Collaboration : KPU employees work in functional and cross-functional teams, coming together to solve complex issues and accomplish objectives that will benefit the KPU community. Please click here for a more detailed job description Salary Information The compensation range is the span between the minimum and maximum base salary (as listed above) for a position.  Approximately halfway between the minimum and the maximum represents an employee that possesses full job knowledge, qualifications and experience for the position.  In the normal course, employees will be hired, transferred or promoted between the minimum and approximately halfway of the salary range for a job. Annual salary increases are available through participation in the Administrative Performance Management program Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4706": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Indigenous Designer-in-Residence Department/Faculty Wilson School of Design Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration Please see details below Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4706 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Director, Strategy and Business Development, Wilson School of Design. SUMMARY The Wilson School of Design (WSD) invites applications from established or emerging Indigenous designers, including First Nations, Métis, and Inuit of Canada, for a position as Indigenous Designer-in-Residence. This residency will support Indigenous designers in the research and creation of new works, and is open to designers in a variety of fields, including but not restricted to fashion and apparel design, graphic design, interior design, product design, and other interdisciplinary design practices. The Indigenous Designer-in-Residence will be able to divide their time between their own creative practice and contributing to the Wilson School of Design. In their application, candidates are encouraged to detail how they envision engaging with the Wilson School of Design and the broader KPU community of faculty, students, and staff. For more information about the Wilson School of Design, please visit our website at https://www.kpu.ca/design. An applicant does not need to have to an expertise in all disciplines, but have at least one expertise and a common fundamental understanding of others. Designers will be compensated for the duration of their residency. There will also be funding available for KPU/WSD-specific events, expenses for materials and supplies, as well as for honoraria for designers whom the Indigenous Designer-in-Residence may want to invite to events. Applications should include: A curriculum vitae or resume A cover letter or video that includes your statement of interest; a proposal of the design project you will undertake during the residency; and a description of the kinds of events you would like to plan, and how you see these contributing to the KPU/WSD community. (For video submissions, please provide a link to a website or Google doc.) Please include a statement clearly indicating your availability to be present on KPU campuses (primarily the Richmond campus). A letter of support or documentation regarding your connections to Indigenous community and/or an Indigenous organization, as well as lived experience. A portfolio: up to 10 original works with titles and dates. Please provide the portfolio through a link to a website; or links to videos or audio files; or a link to a Google doc. The names of two references: One from community and one professional. KPU is committed to the Truth and Reconciliation Commission (TRC) Calls to Action and to supporting Indigenous designers and their representation and visibility within KPU and its broader communities. This program will foster community engagement and will have a positive impact on both the designers and the KPU community through sharing, dialogue, creativity, and intercultural communication. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The organization and hosting of a series of events for the WSD and KPU that may include the following: designer talks/critiques; workshops; studio visits; outreach activities Giving guest lectures, or workshops within the WSD and KPU. Consulting with students and designers of various abilities. Participating in events organized by the WSD and/or KPU Meeting regularly with the Director, Strategy and Business Development, WSD QUALIFICATIONS Relevant community-based and/or professional experience rooted in Indigenous communities, knowledges, and traditions Designers should be active in their design discipline(s) with an established or emerging record of work as made evident through websites, exhibitions, showcases, reviews, articles, etc. A record of participation in the design community and related events Enthusiasm for connecting with KPU’s community members from a variety of areas and disciplines Willingness to organize and plan events in collaboration with the WSD Communications and Events Coordinator. SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly rate: $45.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4721": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Indigenous Residency Support Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 3-6 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4721 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Faculty of Arts. SUMMARY The Student Assistant Indigenous Residency Support will assist the Communication and Events Coordinator on the planning and execution of various KPU and Faculty of Arts (FOA) events related to the Faculty of Arts Indigenous Artist, Writer, Journalist, or Knowledge-Keeper in Residence. These residencies require additional support for events, communication, and administrative assistance while at KPU. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Work under supervision and guidance of the Communications and Events Coordinator. Assist with planning, setup, coordination and operational logistics of FOA and KPU events. Act as a liaison between the residencies and the KPU internal and external community. Attend events to support the residences and engage with current students and community members. Communicate and promote events when appropriate. Document experience, events, and activities with photography and/or film (using video). QUALIFICATIONS Qualified candidates will have an interest in Indigenous arts, writings, and research Familiarity with Indigenous protocols and research methodologies is an asset Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to communicate clearly with others Problem solver, works independently and manages time effectively to meet deadlines This position is reserved for KPU Students only. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4782": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Indigenous Services Student Assistant Department/Faculty Student Services - Indigenous Services for Students Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 4 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4782 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): SUMMARY: Reporting to the Coordinator, Indigenous Student Transition and Engagement, the Student Assistant acts as a peer liaison and host to Indigenous students through one-on-one or small group interactions focusing on creating a safe and welcoming environment and promoting student engagement. The student assistant (also referred to as a Gathering Place Host) also supports a variety of cultural, social, and educational events at KPU. PRINCIPAL DUTIES: Act as a peer liaison to assist students by identifying various KPU student support services and/or make referrals to appropriate departments and/or community organizations Greet and welcome students and guests to the Gathering Place (GP) in a warm and friendly manner Promote student life activities and events Contribute to peer-run bi-monthly email newsletter and social media that highlight scholarship and funding opportunities, campus and community events Support team event planning for Indigenous cultural and community events Assist Coordinator at educational and community events, as needed Monitor GP resources and maintain bulletin board so that it is relevant and organized Assist students in the GP with computers and supplies, as needed Attend weekly departmental team meetings REQUIREMENTS: Applicant must be of Indigenous (First Nations, Métis, or Inuit) ancestry Must be enrolled at KPU as a full time student and in good academic standing Must be familiar with available student support services and campus resources Must have excellent interpersonal skills Must have experience in MS office; and knowledge of online platforms such as Moodle would be considered an asset Ability to multi-task Must be willing to travel to other campus, as needed This position is reserved for KPU Students only. SALARY INFORMATION: Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4502": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Lab Instructor, Faculty of Arts Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration On-Call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4502 Internal Closing Date: March 7, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: 13 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $33.88 to $37.81 per hour Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday Hours of Work (BCGEU): On-Call Hours per Week (BCGEU): On-Call We are currently seeking a Lab Instructor to join the Faculty of Arts Job Overview This position reports to the Divisional Business Manager and works in collaboration with the Department Chair/Coordinator, instructors, and a team of Lab Instructors. The Lab Instructor assists the Faculty of Arts with overall course delivery in designated departments by assuming responsibility for reviewing material with students, student guidance and assessment (including participation in the class and lab component of any course). In addition to instructing students on lab procedures and the use of lab equipment, the Lab Instructor researches, conduct experiments, and introduces new materials, equipment and procedures to advance the program. The Lab Instructor may support any program or course offered by the relevant department(s). The class and lab assignments and learning objectives will be provided by the instructor.  Standard and prescribed industry practices will be created in collaboration between instructors, Lab Instructors, and students.  Using these, Lab Instructors are expected to perform their duties with a minimum of managerial supervision and work effectively with other Lab Instructors, faculty members, student mentors, the KPU community, and the Entertainment Arts industry. Education and Experience Graduation from a 2-year Entertainment Arts program within the past five years is required. Experience tutoring and working with students is an asset Proven junior industry-level proficiency regarding current technology and software used in the Entertainment Arts program(s) Priority will be given to candidates with experience in the specialty area of rigging. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Experience working collaboratively as an effective team player. Proven ability to take initiative when working both independently and as part of a team. Proven ability to juggle and prioritize tasks, work to meet deadlines and demands, make responsible decisions, and determine when to seek advice. Experience developing, planning, and administering systems and/or projects. Demonstrated attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment in making critical decisions. Experience in identifying problems, evaluating alternatives, consulting with stakeholders, and implementing effective solutions. Proven ability to think innovatively and creatively to implement new systems and procedures.  Evaluate their effectiveness. Experience in Microsoft Office suite (e.g. Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, Word). Proven ability to quickly learn new software and equipment as needed. Proven ability to exercise tact, diplomacy, and resolve conflicts. Experience to providing guidance, training, and instruction to others. Demonstrated innovation and change-management skills which include supporting and encouraging new ideas and approaches to build organizational efficiency. Excellent communication, organizational, time management, and interpersonal skills is required. Demonstrated ability to maintain discretion and confidentiality is required. Please click here for a more detailed job description As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4755": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Laboratory Instructor, Biology Department/Faculty Faculty of Science Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration On-Call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4755 Internal Closing Date: August 24, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: 13 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $33.88 to $37.81 per hour Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Flex Hours Required Hours of Work (BCGEU): On-Call (varies) Hours per Week (BCGEU): On-Call (varies) We are currently seeking a Laboratory Instructor, Biology to join our Faculty of Science team. Job Overview The Laboratory Instructor - Biology participates in the Biology Department with the overall course delivery by assuming responsibility for instruction, student guidance and assessment within a lab environment. The Laboratory Instructor - Biology may be assigned to work alongside other Laboratory Instructors (or a faculty member) or alone in fulfilling the above functions. They are expected to perform with a minimum of managerial supervision by the Lab Supervisor and Dean’s Office. Lab responsibilities may involve any university level (first to fourth year) or applied program service courses offered in the Biology Department’s educational plan. Special Considerations: The Biology faculty is ultimately responsible for course delivery and development, including the laboratory portion of any course. The Laboratory Instructor - Biology assists the faculty through their role in the labs in achieving this aim.  The Lab Instructor – Biology and faculty work collegially to meet a common aim. Workload and scheduled contact hours can be found in the “WORKLOAD GUIDELINES FOR FACULTY OF SCIENCE LAB INSTRUCTORS”. The Laboratory Instructor - Biology works in compliance with current WHMIS regulations and directs students in all aspects of lab safety. They must have read the Laboratory Safety and Biosafety Manuals, completed Biosafety and Fire Safety Training and be aware of their potential role and responsibilities in the event of a chemical or biohazardous spill or accident. They must comply with all Biosafety and Biosecurity requirements of the Canadian biosafety standard of the Public Health Agency of Canada while working with Containment Level 2 organisms as it pertains to the department’s pathogens and toxins license. Education and Experience Baccalaureate degree, Masters preferred, in Biology. Proven related teaching experience is an asset. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated good working knowledge of the course content and competence in laboratory techniques pertaining to the instruction of any year biology courses. Demonstrated good working knowledge of the course content and competence in laboratory techniques pertaining to one or more of the following – introduction to biology, cell biology, microbiology, genetics, ecology, botany, marine biology, zoology, anatomy and physiology and human anatomy and physiology. Demonstrated working knowledge of the operation and routine maintenance of laboratory equipment and apparatus. Proven ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing. Demonstrated ability to provide instruction to undergraduate students in a laboratory setting. Demonstrated working knowledge of current WHMIS, biosafety and other preventative measures required for the safe   operation of the biology lab. Proven ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with people of varied background and experience. Proven ability to work in a team-oriented environment. Ability to travel between campuses. Please Note: When applying to this staffing process, you are not applying for a specific job, but to an inventory (or pool) for future on-call vacancies. As vacancies become available, applicants who meet the qualifications will be contacted and may require further assessment depending on the requirements of the assignment. Individuals should have a flexible schedule with the ability to work at any of our five campuses. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
