    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4785": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Research Assistant Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 7 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4785 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): SUMMARY: The student assistant primarily engaged in research with secondary materials will assist faculty or members of the Dean’s office with various research projects. PRINCIPAL DUTIES: Research, editing, and typing of academic journal articles and books Develop and maintain files on issues related to the current project Do library and online research as required (e.g. review current literature, statistics, legal research, academic journals, surveys, online databases, etc.) Assist with photocopying, typing, filing, and overall organization of these materials Work on a variety of initiatives that the Faculty needs assistance with from internal marketing to students, student engagement, course programming Communicate with faculty, peers, relevant internal and external partners as directed by faculty Research, collate, and assist in planning relevant events and identify ways to connect students to alumni and industry as needed Create tracking systems and processes to ensure systems are in place to maintain strategies into the future Research, compile data and write papers to be incorporated into proposals a variety of Faculty purposes Prepare summary reports including headings and information which can be subsequently used to draft briefing notes or craft power point presentations REQUIREMENTS: Ability to follow directions with minimal supervision Demonstrated strong attention to detail and quality deliverables Ability to use MS Office tools, including databases for tracking or qualitative and/or quantitative studies Good interpersonal, organization, research and written skills A professional and positive attitude Knowledge of the research area This position is reserved for KPU Students only. SALARY INFORMATION: Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4790": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Research Assistant, Office of Equity and Inclusive Communities Department/Faculty Office of the Vice President, Equity & Inclusive Communities Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration March, 2027 Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4790 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This position reports to Dr. Asma Sayed, Canada Research Chair in South Asian Literary and Cultural Studies. SUMMARY This is a part-time position for a Research Assistant to work with and report to Canada Research Chair, Dr. Asma Sayed, on a number of research and writing projects based on South Asian literature and cinema. This position requires occasionally working in-person with the supervisor from KPU's Surrey campus. A major or minor in English, Creative Writing, Asian Studies, Film Studies, Social Justice will be given preference. Knowledge of South Asian languages such as Hindi, Gujarati, Punjabi, Urdu, etc. is an asset. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Assisting with organizing conferences, workshops, and symposiums Collaborating with the Research Associate and supporting them Researching/Locating, collating, and annotating key literature Research, editing and typing of academic journal articles and books Develop and maintain files on issues related to the current project Conduct library and online research as required Assist with photocopying, typing, filing, and overall organization of materials Communication with faculty, peers, relevant internal and external partners as directed Prepare summary reports Supporting with writing, citations, and document layout Co-authoring short pieces (author profiles, book reviews) with the supervisor Creating infographics of key findings Support with revising, editing, and analyzing written pieces Amplifying research findings and other relevant details through social media QUALIFICATIONS Qualified candidates will have an interest in and/or knowledge of South Asian literature and cinema, and social justice issues Strong writing and communication skills Completing tasks within assigned deadlines Regular and consistent delivery of assigned tasks Experience with researching, writing, editing Ability to follow direction with minimal supervision Demonstrated strong attention to detail Ability to use MS Office tools including databases for tracking or qualitative and/or quantitative studies Good interpersonal, organization, research skills A professional and positive attitude APPLICATION PROCESS A complete application includes: A resume A statement of interest (300-500 words) that explains why you would like to work on this project A writing sample Please combine the required documents into one single document when submitting your application. *SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $22-$27 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4705": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Research Facilitator Department/Faculty Office of Research and Innovation Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 2 Years Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4705 Internal Closing Date: August 9, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 14 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $34.78 to $38.87 per hour Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 8:30am-4:30pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking a Research Facilitator to join our Office of Research and Innovation team. Job Overview The Office of Research Services (ORS) supports the academic research mission of Kwantlen Polytechnic University, and is responsible for the oversight of all scholarly research activities at KPU, providing assistance and services to all employees and students engaged in research, scholarly activity and creative achievement. As an integral member of the ORS team, the Research Facilitator is responsible for working with research active scholars: to help establish research agendas and build scholarly portfolios; to support research clusters (Institutes or Centres); and to design and facilitate creative approaches and knowledge mobilization strategies to promote KPU research and scholarly activity. The incumbent will liaise with internal and external communities of interest to support researchers with proposal development, source funding and knowledge transfer. This is a temporary full-time position with a term of approximately two years. The position may become continuous subject to funding. Education and Experience A doctorate degree or an equivalent combination of a Master’s degree, training and experience. Previous experience as a researcher in university environment, government projects or agencies is highly desirable. Knowledge of University research and research resources and procedures is an asset. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Expert knowledge of Tri-Agency and other funding opportunities, policies, program requirements and application procedures. Thorough understanding of research processes across different disciplines. Strong computer skills, including the ability to work with a broad range of internal and external information system tools. Exceptional decision-making skills, problem solving abilities, and discretion in handling confidential matters. Exceptional communication (oral and written) and interpersonal skills. Highly motivated and creative to meet the challenges within a complex and evolving university environment. Ability to liaise effectively and diplomatically with a wide variety of internal and external stakeholders and to advocate on behalf of the University and its research community. Strong evidence of success in persuading, influencing and negotiating with peers, colleagues and external contacts. Ability to work to deadlines and prioritize in a demanding work environment. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4739": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Senior Accountant - Financial Reporting Department/Faculty Finance Home Campus (Location) Langley, BC Employment Duration PERMANENT Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4739 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 10 – Administrative Salary Grid - $87,854 to $128,852 Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Administration/Management Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): We are seeking a highly skilled and technically strong Senior Accountant - Financial Reporting to join our Finance team! Job Overview Reporting to the Manager, Financial Reporting, this role serves as a key subject matter expert in financial reporting, accounting standards, and regulatory compliance, supporting KPU’s commitment to financial integrity, transparency, and continuous improvement. The Senior Accountant plays a critical role in the preparation and analysis of complex financial reports and statements, ensuring compliance with Public Sector Accounting Standards, statutory requirements, and KPU policies. This position provides expert guidance on accounting treatment and financial reporting matters, conducts technical research and analysis, develops accounting position papers and recommendations, and supports organizational decision-making through clear and concise communication of complex financial issues. This position is ideal for an experienced accounting professional who thrives in a complex environment, enjoys solving technical accounting challenges, and can confidently translate accounting standards into practical business guidance. The successful candidate will bring strong financial statement preparation experience, a deep understanding of accounting principles and reporting requirements, and the ability to navigate evolving priorities while maintaining a high standard of accuracy and professionalism. Education and Experience Chartered Professional Accountant designation in good standing is required, however candidates working towards the CPA designation or candidates with an equivalent combination of education, training and work experience will be considered; Minimum of two years progressive experience including supervisory and/or managerial experience, as well as a demonstrated ability of effective team management and change and/or systems implementation, resulting in improvements to service quality, staff productivity and systems efficiency; Minimum of three years relevant experience in functional area applied for (Budget/Capital/Operations/Reporting/Research) as well as areas of financial administration, financial systems, projects and assurance; Or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal, with a strong focus on customer service. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels. Proven ability to exercise tact and diplomacy, confidentiality, and conflict resolution skills. Solid understanding of and respect for the diverse values and culture of a university environment. Strong knowledge of accounting procedures and financial reporting practices. Demonstrated ability to summarize and present complex financial data in an organized and concise manner. Strong computer skills, proficiency with spreadsheet programs, and demonstrated ability to use various financial software packages and databases to perform financial analyses and develop reports. Ability to travel between campuses is required. Competencies Leadership: KPU employees inspire, coach, mentor, and support students, employees and KPU as a whole in achieving objectives. Accountability: KPU employees demonstrate fiscal accountability and take ownership for their actions, decisions and results. Continuous Improvement: KPU employees take a creative approach to opportunities, exploring unique ways to create optimal value for the KPU community. Collaboration: KPU employees work in functional and cross-functional teams, coming together to solve complex issues and accomplish objectives that will benefit the KPU community. Salary Information The above compensation range is the span between the minimum and maximum base salary for a position. Typically, initial salary placement is approximately halfway between the minimum and the maximum. This represents an employee that possesses full job knowledge, qualifications and experience for the position. In the normal course, employees will be hired, transferred or promoted between the minimum and approximately halfway of the salary range for a job with consideration given to internal equity. Want to know more? Click here to view the full job description. Application Process To apply for this opportunity, please submit your cover letter and resume as one document via KPU’s Career Centre (click “Career Opportunities”, find the posting, then click “Apply Now”). Please note that applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. The Search Committee will begin to shortlist after August 17, 2026, although the position will remain open until filled. To be considered in the first round of shortlisting, please apply by August 17, 2026. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4696": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Service Learning Student Assistant Department/Faculty Office of the Provost & VP, Academic Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 5 Months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4696 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 14 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Lead Advisor, Work-Integrated Learning. The Lead Advisor, WIL, reports to their respective Dean and works closely with the Associate Vice President, Academic. SUMMARY Service Learning Assistants (SLAs) are paid student leaders who help coordinate and support service learning courses at KPU. SLAs are exceptional student-learners, helping to ensure service learning projects are transformative, meaningful, and reciprocal. SLAs are typically assigned to support 3 service learning courses per semester, working with faculty, students, and community partners. This pilot program is adapted from the Service Learning Assistants program at Tulane University. SLAs typically support 2-3 service learning courses per semester (8-15 hours a week), working with faculty, students and community partners for planning, presentations, orientations, reflections and logistics. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Ongoing problem-solving, mentoring and logistical support for student peers Assisting with end-of-term wrap up, including communication with community partners Assisting with special projects and programs (liaising with community and partnerships) Collecting and documenting relevant service learning course documents Chronicling special events, ongoing projects, student success and partner communication Assisting with student placements and scheduling Developing and maintaining files on issues related to the current project Conducting library and online research as required (e.g. review current literature, statistics, legal research, academic journals, surveys, online databases, etc.) Assisting with photocopying, typing, filing, and overall organization of these materials Leading orientations as needed Participating in monthly or bi-monthly leadership development with other SLAs Communicating with faculty, peers, relevant internal and external partners as directed by faculty Researching, collating, and assisting in planning relevant events Preparing summary reports including headings and information which can be subsequently used to Drafting briefing notes or craft power point presentations QUALIFICATIONS Must be enrolled, or intend to be enrolled, as a student at KPU during their placement Must be in good academic standing for the term prior to selection Must maintain at least a cumulative GPA of 3.0 Students must be nominated prior to submitting an application form (students can self-nominate). Nominated students, if chosen, will be asked to submit a full application Students must demonstrate experience in service learning or community service; and commit to participate in required orientation and ongoing training Students are expected to be available the week prior to classes that term, for training and to learn about their placements Ability to follow directions with minimal supervision Ability to demonstrate professionalism and email etiquette Awareness of needs around student and partner confidentiality Demonstrated strong attention to detail and quality deliverables Ability to use MS Office tools, including databases Comfort with technology, familiarity with online collaborative tools and platforms Ability to work on a variety of initiatives, flexible and adaptable Good interpersonal, organization, research and written skills A professional and positive attitude Preference, in some cases, may go to students who have already completed a service learning course (e.g. worked with community partners) Preference, in some cases, may go to students who speak additional languages Preference, in some cases, may go to students who have familiarity with Canva or similar poster-making platforms This position is reserved for KPU Students only. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4781": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Social Media Student Ambassador – KPU International Department/Faculty International Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 7 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4781 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Communications and Events Coordinator, KPU International. SUMMARY The Social Media Student Ambassador is integral to KPU International and enhances the KPU student experience with prospective and current international students and community members. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Work closely with the KPU International Communication and Events team. Engage on social media platforms in a professional, friendly, and approachable manner. Assist with content for divisional social media platforms. Assist with photo and video recording during KPU International events. Represent KPU International on social media platforms. QUALIFICATIONS Good academic standing. Good organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Experience in communications, marketing, and/or a related field is an asset. Proficient in MS Office applications. Familiar with common social media platforms such as creating video content and social media posts Be comfortable with being on camera and filming video content for social media platforms. Reliable, responsible, and professional with a customer-service mindset. Able to work independently and as part of a team. Able to effectively multi-task. Sensitive to the needs of a diverse student population. Available to work across all KPU campuses as needed. Available to work evenings and weekends as needed. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
