    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4166": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Tutors - Student Assistant - Learning Centre Department/Faculty Faculty of Academic & Career Preparation Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 8 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4166 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 44 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Learning Strategist or Learning Centre Coordinator. SUMMARY Tutors receive three levels of training. Principle duties include tutoring KPU students to help them become more effective learners. Tutors achieve this by asking questions about the student's understanding of the subject area, making suggestions about how to study or a method of approaching a problem, modelling appropriate learning strategies, and by referring the student to learning resources or other services within or outside the university. Peer Tutors are not expected to teach coursework. They are not expected to be substitutes for teachers and they are definitely not allowed to do the student's work or assignments. Peer tutors are current KPU students helping other students to learn. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES To tutor KPU students in specific subject areas after completing appropriate training To help KPU students to understand main course concepts, how to follow assignment structures, and how to improve their performance in their coursework To provide feedback on students' assignments and to provide students with ways to improve their work To help students to identify and find the assistance they need To assist with transition, orientation and retention programs To assist with the promotion of Learning Centre services and programs QUALIFICATIONS Confident in their knowledge of a specific subject(s) Patient and willing to tailor their explanation of key concepts to a variety of students Friendly and welcoming of all students Punctual, focused, and hard-working Be registered as a KPU student Maintain a minimum GPA of 3.0 and have completed at least 24 credit hours Provide references from two KPU instructors who would support your application Can identify ways in which to learn subject matter effectively Can identify errors in students' understanding of key course concepts Has a clear understanding of the key concepts and skills in the courses and subject areas that they wish to tutor in LOCATION KPU has four learning centers, which are located on the Surrey, Langley, Richmond, and Cloverdale campuses. Tutors can choose which campus they would like to tutor at; however, different tutors are needed at different campuses depending on the subject that they tutor in. Tutors will also be eligible to tutor online. This position is reserved for KPU students only. *APPLICATION PROCESS All applications must include: Resume Unofficial Transcript Next Semester Course Schedule Reference Letter *Required documents must be combined into one single document when uploading to your application. *SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4443": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Welding Instructor Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 (one) year on call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4443 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Qualified Faculty List Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): WELDING INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: Qualified Faculty List POSITION START: As soon as possible FACULTY OVERVIEW: Kwantlen Polytechnic University’s Welding program provides students with the necessary training to become professional welders. Students will develop the skill and knowledge to work safely and effectively in today’s demanding industrial environment. POSITION OVERVIEW: The Faculty of Trades and Technology is currently seeking a Non-regular Type 1 Welding Instructor to provide short-term delivery of Apprenticeship Levels 1, 2, and 3, Welding Foundation and/or Levels B and A which may extend from a single day to several weeks. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: British Columbia Certificate of Qualification with Interprovincial Red Seal Endorsement. Current BC Pipe Welder Pressure Vessel 7 (PWP7) and BC Pipe Welder Pressure Vessel 10 (PWP10) pressure tickets, or equivalent. A minimum of five years’ experience working in the industry as a journeyperson. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates will be required to undergo a Criminal Record Check. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, our faculty will draw on our Qualified Faculty List to assign work, please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4787": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Wilson School of Design Student Assistant (Generalist with Specializations) Department/Faculty Wilson School of Design Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 3.5 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4787 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 10 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Wilson School of Design Dean’s Office. SUMMARY The Student Assistant supports a range of activities within the Wilson School of Design (WSD), contributing to student success, operations, and community engagement. This role is designed as a flexible, multi-functional position, where students may work across different areas or be assigned a primary specialization based on skills, experience, and operational needs. Student Assistants play a key role in fostering a welcoming, inclusive, and dynamic environment by supporting student learning, events, communications, labs, and peer engagement initiatives. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES (for all Student Assistants) Represent WSD as a positive, professional ambassador at events and within the community Provide excellent customer service and respectful, timely support to students, faculty, staff, and visitors Assist with general operational tasks including setup, coordination, and logistics Support promotion and communication of WSD activities and resources Maintain organized, safe, and welcoming environments across spaces and activities Work both independently and collaboratively while managing time effectively Attend training sessions, team meetings, and professional development opportunities as required Perform additional related duties as assigned AREAS OF SPECIALIZATION Students hired for this position will be assigned to the Peer Mentorship and Student Engagement stream in support of the Wilson Collective initiative. You may be asked to support one of the other streams if needed. 1. Peer Mentorship & Student Engagement Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Provide peer support, guidance, and mentorship to students Share information about academic resources, student services, and wellness supports Foster a sense of belonging and community among WSD students Participate in outreach, community-building initiatives, and student engagement 2. Events & Communications Support Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Assist with planning, coordination, and execution of events (e.g., recruitment, community, student life) Support event logistics including setup, takedown, and on-site coordination Engage with current and prospective students and external community members Contribute to the promotion and documentation of events (photography/video/social media) for web platforms 3. Labs & Technical/Studio Support Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Provide general support for lab, workshop, and studio activities Assist with non-specialized preparation and set-up tasks for classes, projects, and events Help communicate established procedures and direct students to appropriate resources Assist with tours, exhibitions, displays, installations, and special events Observe and report equipment, facility, or safety concerns to supervisory staff Support equipment use and lab operations that are supportive in nature QUALIFICATIONS Currently enrolled student at the Wilson School of Design Strong oral and written communication and interpersonal skills Organized, reliable, self-motivated, and detail-oriented Ability to work independently and collaboratively Comfortable engaging with diverse audiences and communities Interest in student life, community engagement, or design environments ASSETS (vary by specialization): Experience with events, communications, or social media Experience in peer mentoring or leadership roles Familiarity with lab equipment, tools, or creative production processes Working knowledge of Microsoft Office, Adobe Creative Cloud, and WordPress This position is reserved for KPU students only. *SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4800": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Position Description New Search Log-in Page Position Description Wilson School of Design Student Assistant (Generalist with Specializations) Department/Faculty Wilson School of Design Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 6.5 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4800 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 7 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Wilson School of Design Dean’s Office. SUMMARY The Student Assistant supports a range of activities within the Wilson School of Design (WSD), contributing to student success, operations, and community engagement. This role is designed as a flexible, multi-functional position, where students may work across different areas or be assigned a primary specialization based on skills, experience, and operational needs. Student Assistants play a key role in fostering a welcoming, inclusive, and dynamic environment by supporting student learning, events, communications, labs, and peer engagement initiatives. The following positions are available: Events & Communication Support : 2 vacancies Labs and Technical/Studio Support: 2 vacancies (Workshop) 2 vacancies (Studios and Production Labs) 1 vacancy (Textiles Lab) Applicants are required to indicate their interest in one (or more) of the above positions. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Core Responsibilities (All Student Assistants): Represent WSD as a positive, professional ambassador at events and within the community. Provide excellent customer service and respectful, timely support to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Assist with general operational tasks including setup, coordination, and logistics. Support promotion and communication of WSD activities and resources. Maintain organized, safe, and welcoming environments across spaces and activities. Work both independently and collaboratively while managing time effectively. Attend training sessions, team meetings, and professional development opportunities as required. Perform additional related duties as assigned. AREAS OF SPECIALIZATION Student Assistants will be assigned to one of the following streams and may be asked to support in other streams if needed. 1. Peer Mentorship & Student Engagement Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Provide peer support, guidance, and mentorship to students. Share information about academic resources, student services, and wellness supports. Foster a sense of belonging and community among WSD students. Participate in outreach, community-building initiatives, and student engagement 2. Events & Communications Support Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Assist with planning, coordination, and execution of events (e.g., recruitment, community, student life). Support event logistics including setup, takedown, and on-site coordination. Engage with current and prospective students and external community members. Contribute to the promotion and documentation of events (photography/video/social media) for web platforms. 3. Labs & Technical/Studio Support Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Provide general support for lab, workshop, and studio activities. Assist with non-specialized preparation and set-up tasks for classes, projects, and events. Help communicate established procedures and direct students to appropriate resources. Assist with tours, exhibitions, displays, installations, and special events. Observe and report equipment, facility, or safety concerns to supervisory staff. Support equipment use and lab operations that are supportive in nature. QUALIFICATIONS Currently enrolled student at the Wilson School of Design. Strong oral and written communication and interpersonal skills. Organized, reliable, self-motivated, and detail-oriented. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Comfortable engaging with diverse audiences and communities. Interest in student life, community engagement, or design environments. Assets (vary by specialization): Experience with events, communications, or social media. Experience in peer mentoring or leadership roles. Familiarity with lab equipment, tools, or creative production processes. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office, Adobe Creative Cloud, and WordPress. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
